From a78786207672b9aab7880979da41df62e6e6fde8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris O'Hearn <137103567+chrisohearn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:50:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] device-manager: Tell the daemon before freeing a renderer's
 keyboard

free_keyboards_for_renderer() frees each keyboard that belongs to a
removed renderer, but never calls keyboard_removed_handler, so the
daemon and the splash plugin keep a pointer to the freed keyboard. When
the splash is hidden after that (for example plymouth quit right after
simpledrm hands over to the real DRM driver), the script plugin calls
ply_keyboard_remove_input_handler() on freed memory and plymouthd
crashes with SIGSEGV.

Call keyboard_removed_handler before ply_keyboard_free(), as
keyboard_added_handler is called when the keyboard is created.

Signed-off-by: Chris O'Hearn <137103567+chrisohearn@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git i/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c w/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
index aacab4d3..58adbdf1 100644
--- i/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
+++ w/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
@@ -168,2 +168,5 @@ free_keyboards_for_renderer (ply_device_manager_t *manager,
                 if (keyboard_renderer == renderer) {
+                        if (manager->keyboard_removed_handler != NULL)
+                                manager->keyboard_removed_handler (manager->event_handler_data, keyboard);
+
                         ply_keyboard_free (keyboard);
